# Code Ownership
# Defines who reviews changes to specific files/directories
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# AI-First Strategy:
# - No blanket ownership (enables auto-merge for routine work)
# - Strategic files require human review (foundation, config, workflows, decisions)
# - Balance between AI autonomy and strategic oversight

# Foundation and core configuration
# Strategic documents require human review
/FOUNDATION.md @jcmrs
/LICENSE @jcmrs
/docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md @jcmrs
/config/ @jcmrs

# GitHub configuration
# Changes to workflows, templates, and automation
/.github/ @jcmrs

# Documentation
# AI can propose, human reviews for alignment
# EXCEPTION: Perplexity research prompts auto-merge (external consultation requests)
/docs/PERPLEXITY_PROMPT_*.md

# Strategic documentation requires review
/docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md @jcmrs
/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md @jcmrs
/docs/DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md @jcmrs

# Other documentation can be reviewed by AI agents
/docs/

# Decisions
# All ADRs should be reviewed
/decisions/ @jcmrs

# Requirements
# Specification changes need oversight
/requirements/ @jcmrs
